{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-001","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 1","quote_original":"Unconditioned consciousness is God, the one and only reality. By unconditioned consciousness is meant a sense of awareness; a sense of knowing that I AM apart from knowing who I AM; the consciousness of being, divorced from that which I am conscious of being.","primary_topic":"CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM","secondary_topics":["SPIRITUAL"],"tags":["awareness","i-am","consciousness"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-002","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 1","quote_original":"I AM the unconditioned reality conditioned as that which I believe myself to be. I AM the believer limited by my beliefs, the knower defined by the known.","primary_topic":"CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM","secondary_topics":["SELF_CONCEPT"],"tags":["i-am","beliefs","self-concept"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-003","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 1","quote_original":"The world is my conditioned consciousness objectified. That which I feel and believe to be true of myself is now projected in space as my world. The world – my mirrored self – ever bears witness of the state of consciousness in which I live.","primary_topic":"REALITY_CIRCUMSTANCES","secondary_topics":["CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM","SELF_CONCEPT"],"tags":["world","mirror","consciousness","belief"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-004","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 1","quote_original":"One day man will realize that his own I AM-ness is the God he has been seeking throughout the ages, and that his own sense of awareness – his consciousness of being – is the one and only reality.","primary_topic":"CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM","secondary_topics":["SPIRITUAL"],"tags":["i-am","awareness","god"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-005","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 1","quote_original":"Name God by consciously defining yourself as your highest ideal.","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","secondary_topics":["SPIRITUAL"],"tags":["highest-ideal","self-definition","god"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-006","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 2","quote_original":"Conditioned consciousness continually objectifies itself on the screen of space.","primary_topic":"CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM","secondary_topics":["REALITY_CIRCUMSTANCES"],"tags":["objectification","consciousness","space"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-007","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 2","quote_original":"The world is the image and likeness of the subjective conscious state which created it.","primary_topic":"REALITY_CIRCUMSTANCES","secondary_topics":["CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM"],"tags":["subjective-state","world","creation"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-008","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 2","quote_original":"Believing is simply living in the feeling of actually being the state imagined – by assuming the consciousness of being the state desired.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","secondary_topics":["FEELING","CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM"],"tags":["belief","feeling","state-desired"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-009","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 2","quote_original":"First, you are aware; then you become aware of something; then you become aware as that which you were aware of; then you behold objectively that which you are aware of being.","primary_topic":"CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM","secondary_topics":["ASSUMPTION","REALITY_CIRCUMSTANCES"],"tags":["awareness","being","objectification"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-010","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 3","quote_original":"The conscious union or mystical marriage is made possible only through feeling.","primary_topic":"FEELING","secondary_topics":["ASSUMPTION"],"tags":["feeling","union","mystical-marriage"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-011","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 3","quote_original":"To feel the presence of the thing desired, to subjectively actualize a state by impressing upon yourself, through feeling, a definite conscious state is the secret of creation.","primary_topic":"FEELING","secondary_topics":["DESIRE","ASSUMPTION"],"tags":["feeling","desired-state","creation"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-012","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 3","quote_original":"Consciousness calls things that are not seen as though they were, and it does this by first defining itself as that which it desires to express, and second by remaining within the defined state until the invisible becomes visible.","primary_topic":"CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM","secondary_topics":["ASSUMPTION","DESIRE"],"tags":["defined-state","invisible","consciousness"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-013","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 3","quote_original":"Don’t question how it can be done; simply feel that you have it. Assume the attitude of mind that would be yours if you were already in possession of it so that you feel that it is done.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","secondary_topics":["FEELING","DESIRE"],"tags":["how","possession","feeling-it-done"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-014","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 3","quote_original":"Feeling is the secret of creation.","primary_topic":"FEELING","secondary_topics":["ASSUMPTION"],"tags":["feeling","creation","secret"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-015","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 4","quote_original":"Your consciousness is the cause of your world. The conscious state in which you abide determines the kind of world in which you live.","primary_topic":"CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM","secondary_topics":["REALITY_CIRCUMSTANCES"],"tags":["cause","world","state"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-016","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 4","quote_original":"You do not see your desire objectively; you simply sense it (feel it) subjectively.","primary_topic":"FEELING","secondary_topics":["DESIRE"],"tags":["desire","subjective","feeling"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-017","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 4","quote_original":"You do not make a mental journey; you collapse space. Sit quietly where you are and make “there-ness” “here-ness.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","secondary_topics":["FEELING"],"tags":["there-ness","here-ness","imaginal-location"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-018","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 5","quote_original":"The Sabbath is the mental rest which follows the fixed psychological state. It is the result of your six days of work.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","secondary_topics":["FAITH_PRAYER"],"tags":["sabbath","mental-rest","fixed-state"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-019","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 5","quote_original":"Pregnancy follows impregnation. Man does not continue desiring that which he has already acquired.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","secondary_topics":["DESIRE"],"tags":["sabbath","acquired","desire"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-020","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 5","quote_original":"Man has been stirred out of his sleep through the medium of desire, and can find no rest until he realizes his desire.","primary_topic":"DESIRE","secondary_topics":["ASSUMPTION"],"tags":["desire","rest","realization"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-021","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 6","quote_original":"Every problem reveals its own solution.","primary_topic":"REALITY_CIRCUMSTANCES","secondary_topics":["DESIRE"],"tags":["problem","solution"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-022","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 6","quote_original":"You impress upon yourself the fact that you are that which you desire to be until your mind is stilled in the belief that it is so.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","secondary_topics":["DESIRE","FEELING"],"tags":["impression","belief","stillness"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-023","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 7","quote_original":"Change your conception of yourself and you will automatically change the nature of your desires.","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","secondary_topics":["DESIRE"],"tags":["self-concept","desire","change"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-024","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 7","quote_original":"Desires are states of consciousness seeking embodiment. They are formed by man’s consciousness and can easily be expressed by the man who has conceived them.","primary_topic":"DESIRE","secondary_topics":["CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM"],"tags":["desire","state","embodiment"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-025","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 7","quote_original":"Always hear and accept as true of others that which you would desire for yourself. In so doing, you are building heaven on earth.","primary_topic":"RELATIONSHIPS","secondary_topics":["DESIRE"],"tags":["others","golden-rule","heaven-on-earth"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-026","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 7","quote_original":"You turn your attention from your present conception of yourself and assume the consciousness of being that which you want to be, thereby passing from one state to another.","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","secondary_topics":["ASSUMPTION","CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM"],"tags":["attention","state-change","self-concept"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-027","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 8","quote_original":"Faith is feeling or living in the consciousness of being the thing desired.","primary_topic":"FAITH_PRAYER","secondary_topics":["FEELING","ASSUMPTION"],"tags":["faith","feeling","desired-state"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-028","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 8","quote_original":"How would you feel if you were that which you desire to be?","primary_topic":"FEELING","secondary_topics":["DESIRE","ASSUMPTION"],"tags":["feeling","desire","question"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-029","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 8","quote_original":"Wear the mood, this feeling that would be yours if you were already that which you desire to be; and in a little while you will be sealed in the belief that you are.","primary_topic":"FEELING","secondary_topics":["ASSUMPTION","DESIRE"],"tags":["mood","belief","wish-fulfilled"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-030","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 9","quote_original":"You select the person in your world who would be sincerely thrilled in witnessing the fulfillment of your desire.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","secondary_topics":["RELATIONSHIPS","DESIRE"],"tags":["imaginal-conversation","friend","fulfillment"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-031","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 9","quote_original":"With your desire properly defined, you assume an attitude of listening. Imagine you are hearing the voice of a friend; then make him tell you (imagine he is telling you) how lucky and fortunate you are to have fully realized your desire.","primary_topic":"IMAGINATION","secondary_topics":["INNER_CONVERSATION","DESIRE"],"tags":["listening","friend-voice","imaginal-conversation"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"FFA-CUR-032","corpus_id":"B003","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"Freedom For All","source_year":1942,"source_slug":"freedom_for_all","source_section":"Chapter 9","quote_original":"The emotional thrill of having heard that which you desire to hear is the moment of conception.","primary_topic":"FEELING","secondary_topics":["INNER_CONVERSATION","DESIRE"],"tags":["emotional-thrill","hearing","conception"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_freedom_for_all.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
